e.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?\">toOrdinal?</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option.none\">none</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?_eq_none","kind":"theorem","line":257,"name":"Float32.toOrdinal?_eq_none","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L257-L258"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?_eq_some\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal?_eq_some</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">h</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?\">toOrdinal?</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option.some\">some</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal\">toOrdinal</a></span> <span class=\"fn\">h</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?_eq_some","kind":"theorem","line":254,"name":"Float32.toOrdinal?_eq_some","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L254-L255"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance!\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulpDistance!</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The distance between `x` and `y` in units in the last place, as in `ulpDistance`.\nPanics when either argument is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance!","kind":"def","line":250,"name":"Float32.ulpDistance!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L250-L252"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance?\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulpDistance?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The distance between `x` and `y` in units in the last place, as in `ulpDistance`, or\n`none` when either argument is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance?","kind":"def","line":247,"name":"Float32.ulpDistance?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L247-L248"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulpDistance</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hx</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hy</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">y</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The number of floating-point numbers between `x` and `y`, counting one of the endpoints: the\ndistance between them in units in the last place. Both zeros count as the same point and the\ninfinities are one step beyond the largest finite numbers. Neither argument may be `NaN`; see\nalso `ulpDistance?` and `ulpDistance!`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulpDistance","kind":"def","line":243,"name":"Float32.ulpDistance","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L243-L245"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal!\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal!</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, as in\n`toOrdinal`. Panics when `x` is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal!","kind":"def","line":240,"name":"Float32.toOrdinal!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L240-L241"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, as in\n`toOrdinal`, or `none` when `x` is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal?","kind":"def","line":237,"name":"Float32.toOrdinal?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L237-L238"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, with both zeros at\n`0`, positive numbers at their bit pattern and negative numbers at the negation of the bit\npattern of their absolute value. Infinities sit one step past the largest finite numbers.\n`x` must not be `NaN`; see also `toOrdinal?` and `toOrdinal!`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.toOrdinal","kind":"def","line":232,"name":"Float32.toOrdinal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L232-L235"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulp\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulp</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The unit in the last place of `x`: the distance from `|x|` to the next number of larger\nmagnitude. For the largest finite number, it is the distance to the next number of smaller\nmagnitude. This agrees with Julia's `eps(x)`.\n\nSpecial cases: `ulp 0` is the smallest positive subnormal number, and `ulp x = nan` when `x` is\ninfinite or `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.ulp","kind":"def","line":217,"name":"Float32.ulp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L217-L230"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.nextDown\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">nextDown</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The greatest floating-point number that compares less than `x`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.1.\n\nThis is `-nextUp (-x)`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.nextDown","kind":"def","line":215,"name":"Float32.nextDown","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L215-L215"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.nextUp\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">nextUp</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The least floating-point number that compares greater than `x`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.1.\n\nSpecial cases: `nextUp nan = nan`, `nextUp inf = inf`, `nextUp (-inf)` is the most negative\nfinite number, and `nextUp` of either zero is the smallest positive subnormal number.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.nextUp","kind":"def","line":207,"name":"Float32.nextUp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L207-L213"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.copySign\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">copySign</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The value `x` with the sign of `y`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.5.1.\n\n`NaN` inputs follow `signBit`: `copySign nan y = nan` and `copySign x nan` has a positive sign.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.copySign","kind":"def","line":203,"name":"Float32.copySign","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L203-L205"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.signBit\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">signBit</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether the sign bit of `x` is set, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.7.2 `isSignMinus`.\n\nThis is `true` for `-0` and `false` for `NaN`, since Lean's floats have a single `NaN` value.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.signBit","kind":"def","line":200,"name":"Float32.signBit","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L200-L201"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.isSubnormal\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSubnormal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether `x` is a subnormal number.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.isSubnormal","kind":"def","line":197,"name":"Float32.isSubnormal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L197-L198"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.isNormal\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">isNormal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether `x` is a normal number: finite, nonzero and not subnormal.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.isNormal","kind":"def","line":194,"name":"Float32.isNormal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L194-L195"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.classify\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">classify</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float32.html#Float32\">Float32</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.Category\">Float.Category</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The class of `x`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.7.2.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.classify","kind":"def","line":186,"name":"Float32.classify","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L186-L192"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.significandMask\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">significandMask</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt32\">UInt32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The significand field of a `Float32`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.significandMask","kind":"def","line":183,"name":"Float32.significandMask","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L183-L184"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.exponentMask\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">exponentMask</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt32\">UInt32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The exponent field of a `Float32`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.exponentMask","kind":"def","line":180,"name":"Float32.exponentMask","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L180-L181"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.signMask\"><span class=\"name\">Float32</span>.<span class=\"name\">signMask</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt32\">UInt32</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The sign bit of a `Float32`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float32.signMask","kind":"def","line":177,"name":"Float32.signMask","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L177-L178"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.ulpDistance!_eq\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulpDistance!_eq</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_