.html#Float.ulpDistance\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulpDistance</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hx</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">hy</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">y</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The number of floating-point numbers between `x` and `y`, counting one of the endpoints: the\ndistance between them in units in the last place. Both zeros count as the same point and the\ninfinities are one step beyond the largest finite numbers. Neither argument may be `NaN`; see\nalso `ulpDistance?` and `ulpDistance!`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.ulpDistance","kind":"def","line":133,"name":"Float.ulpDistance","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L133-L141"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal!\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal!</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, as in\n`toOrdinal`. Panics when `x` is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal!","kind":"def","line":128,"name":"Float.toOrdinal!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L128-L131"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal?\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal?</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, as in\n`toOrdinal`, or `none` when `x` is `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal?","kind":"def","line":123,"name":"Float.toOrdinal?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L123-L126"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">toOrdinal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">x</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float.isNaN\">isNaN</a></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a> → <a href=\"./Init/Data/Int/Basic.html#Int\">Int</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The position of `x` on the number line that counts floating-point numbers, with both zeros at\n`0`, positive numbers at their bit pattern and negative numbers at the negation of the bit\npattern of their absolute value. Infinities sit one step past the largest finite numbers.\n`x` must not be `NaN`; see also `toOrdinal?` and `toOrdinal!`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.toOrdinal","kind":"def","line":113,"name":"Float.toOrdinal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L113-L121"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.ulp\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">ulp</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The unit in the last place of `x`: the distance from `|x|` to the next number of larger\nmagnitude. For the largest finite number, it is the distance to the next number of smaller\nmagnitude. This agrees with Julia's `eps(x)`.\n\nSpecial cases: `ulp 0` is the smallest positive subnormal number, and `ulp x = nan` when `x` is\ninfinite or `NaN`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.ulp","kind":"def","line":98,"name":"Float.ulp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L98-L111"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.nextDown\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">nextDown</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The greatest floating-point number that compares less than `x`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.1.\n\nThis is `-nextUp (-x)`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.nextDown","kind":"def","line":91,"name":"Float.nextDown","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L91-L96"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.nextUp\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">nextUp</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The least floating-point number that compares greater than `x`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.3.1.\n\nSpecial cases: `nextUp nan = nan`, `nextUp inf = inf`, `nextUp (-inf)` is the most negative\nfinite number, and `nextUp` of either zero is the smallest positive subnormal number.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.nextUp","kind":"def","line":77,"name":"Float.nextUp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L77-L89"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.copySign\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">copySign</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x </span><span class=\"fn\">y</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The value `x` with the sign of `y`, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.5.1.\n\n`NaN` inputs follow `signBit`: `copySign nan y = nan` and `copySign x nan` has a positive sign.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.copySign","kind":"def","line":68,"name":"Float.copySign","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L68-L75"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.signBit\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">signBit</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether the sign bit of `x` is set, as in IEEE 754-2019 §5.7.2 `isSignMinus`.\n\nThis is `true` for `-0` and `false` for `NaN`, since Lean's floats have a single `NaN` value.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.signBit","kind":"def","line":60,"name":"Float.signBit","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L60-L66"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.isSubnormal\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSubnormal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether `x` is a subnormal number.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.isSubnormal","kind":"def","line":57,"name":"Float.isSubnormal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L57-L58"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.isNormal\"><span class=\"name\">Float</span>.<span class=\"name\">isNormal</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Data/Float/Float.html#Float\">Float</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Whether `x` is a normal number: finite, nonzero and not subnormal.","docLink":"./Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.html#Float.isNormal","kind":"def","line":54,"name":"Float.isNormal","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Data/Float/Bits.lean#L54-L55"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\"